# Commit and Push by Default

- A request to change this project includes authorization to commit the
  completed work and push it to the current tracked remote branch.
- Run the relevant tests and review the diff before committing.
- Do not commit or push if the request appears mistaken, unsafe, harmful,
  or produces a clearly worse result. Explain the concern and ask first.
- If a push fails, diagnose and retry safe transport fixes; verify that the
  remote commit matches local HEAD before reporting completion.
- Never force-push, rewrite shared history, or include unrelated user
  changes unless the developer explicitly asks.

